   Planning \& Environm; Environ; TAMOIL; UFZ; Deltares; TNO; Prov Milano},
Abstract = {From 1998-2005, Quebec ran a successful urban contaminated site
   revitalisation program called Revi-Sols. A new program, ClimatSol, took
   over in September 2007. Besides fostering contaminated site
   rehabilitation and economic activity as Rev/-Sols did, ClimatSol also
   aim to:
   integrate green technologies to construction projects;
   maintain or create wooden or green surfaces;
   foster Smart Grow and;
   contribute to the fight against global warming
   Even if the program is still at the starting phase, the number of
   municipal and private party proposals received to date indicate that
   ClimatSol fills stakeholders needs and that it could well be possible to
   link contaminated sites revitalisation with a set of ``greening
   measures{''} contributing to fight global warming and add greenness to
   the urban environment.},
