Organization = {Univ Szczecin, Inst Marine \& Coastal Sci; Coastal Educ \& Res Fdn; Univ
   Szczecinski (US); Cztowiek Nauka Srodowisko (CNS); ZMGM; Reg Dyrekcja
   Ochrony Srodowiska; Esri; Springer; Lotos; GA2 Syst; World Sci;
   Helmholtz-Zentrum Geesthacht; Nfosigm; Urzad Marszalkowski Wojewodztwa
   Zachodniopomorskiego; Wojewodzki Fundusz Ochrony Srodowiska I Gospodarki
   Wodnej W Gdansku},
Abstract = {Silva, K. S., Krueger, C. P., Leandro, D. and Huinca, S. C. M., 2011.
   Definition of irregular areas and generation subsidies for verification
   the consequences by human intervention to the environment in coastal
   regions. SI 64 (Proceedings of the 11th International Coastal
   Symposium), 1811 - 1814. Szczecin, Poland, ISSN 0749-0208
   Irregular occupations occur in the cities, in empty lots or even in
   non-urbanized areas. The impasse created by irregular occupation and the
   waiting for a solution to the problem have generated series of urban
   deprivation, leading to instability of the water supply system, sewer,
   electricity, public transportation, road systems, housing deficit and
   occupations risk. In Brazil there are large human settlements in coastal
   areas, which may contribute with the development of irregular
   occupation. At coastal areas the problems generated are even more
   worrying, since they are areas formed by complex ecosystems, which are
   in constant change, with an intense dynamic. Within this context the
   Laboratory of Space Geodesy - LAGE, located in the Polytechnic Center at
   Federal University of Parana, Curitiba - Parana - Brazil, has developed
   a methodology for irregular delimitation of areas that will provide
   subsidies to find the problems created by human intervention to the
   environment. This methodology was proved effective in a permanent
   preservation area, the Vossoroca's reservoir and will eventually be
   applied in coastal regions.},
