   A\&M Int Univ, Laredo, TX, MAY 22-25, 2011},
Organization = {Soc Risk Anal Europe; Soc Risk Anal Japan; Korean Soc Environm Toxicol},
Abstract = {In this work the current situation of nanotechnology in Chile respect to
   the associated risks to the incorporation of this new technology in time
   is analyzed, considering the particularity of Chile and its position in
   Science and Technology field. To know the perception considering the
   risks involved it applies an opinion survey and also a decision tree is
   built in order to take a decision regarding the most prominent risks,
   which there will be that to face upon, having as a main objective a
   greater development to Chilean level to the year 2020, the challenges
   also include technological development as well their impact in the
   economic environment associated. It is concluded that the main risks are
   related to the non-existence of a legislation and/or regulation in
   Sci-Tech field in Chile, which generates absence of feature and
   leadership, and therefore a deficit in the construction of knowledgemeat
   which are determinant factors in the world economic dynamics. It is
   found that in Chile the groups of specialists prepared to face the topic
   are reduced. Finally it is established that a communication strategy
   should exist to report and educate the citizenship, which is of vital
   importance to establish the public policies and regulations on the
   subject.},
