Note = {International Symposium on Social Sciences, Arts and Humanities
   (SYSSARM), Bali, INDONESIA, SEP 29-OCT 01, 2015},
Abstract = {The objective of this study is to analyze the perception of the factors
   that affect the intention of adopting e-commerce by micro enterprises
   through the business value. The factors include relative advantage, ease
   of use, security, cost, managerial characteristic, external pressure,
   managerial behavior towards e-commerce, and trust. The results show that
   relative advantage, ease of use, managerial characteristic, and trust
   influence on the business value, while security, cost, external
   pressure, and managerial behavior towards e-commerce do not. Next, the
   business value influences on the intention of adopting e-commerce.},
