   Peking Univ, Beijing, PEOPLES R CHINA, OCT 19-21, 2009},
Organization = {Soc Risk Anal Europe; Soc Risk Anal Europe; Soc Risk Anal Japan; China
   Assoc Disaster Prevent, Risk Anal Council},
Abstract = {We investigated the particle mass size distributions and chemical
   properties in the urban area and the capacity of air pollution
   particulate matter (PM) to induce cytotoxic in human bronchial
   epithelial (BEAS-2B) cells. The PM size distributions were bi-modal
   (0.18-0.32 and 1.83.2mm). The proportion of the heavy metals for fine
   particles (0.1-1.8um) accounted for 45.6-80.4\% of the mass
   concentrations of metals in PM10. We observed PM concentration-dependent
   cell death rate and release of cytokines (IL-6 and IL-8) in BEAS-2B
   cells. The combined results support the hypothesis that ultrafine
   particles from vehicle sources can induce inflammatory response related
   to environmental respiratory injury.},
