   Changsha, PEOPLES R CHINA, NOV 16, 2009},
Organization = {Sustainable Dev City Grp; Cent S Univ, Hunan Inst Syst Engn \&
   Management},
Abstract = {Railway network of city group can be divided into three layers,
   including urban railway, suburban railway and intercity railway. It's
   difficult to form a natural whole network due to the differences of
   construction timing, investors, operators and standard specifications of
   these railways. From the point of view of ownership and usufruct,
   Investing and operating the railways in the different layers is one of
   the key issues of how to integrate railway resource of city group.
   First of all, study the investment, operation and management of railway
   network in Tokyo City Group, Paris City Group and London City Group one
   by one, and then summarize five company organization modes form them;
   meanwhile, analyze their transplant to China under public ownership and
   the advantages and disadvantages of these transplanted modes. On this
   basis, discuss the adaptability of the five modes to achieve integration
   of railway resource, and then find out that the ``public-managed{''}
   modes are effective ones. Finally, combine the status quo of railway in
   China, and study the investment, operation, management and capacity
   assignment for rebuilding the suburban railway line with superfluous
   transport capacity to join the urban railway system. The results provide
   decision supports for the government to build adapted companies to run
   railway lines after integration.},
