Note = {International Conference on Water Resource and Environmental Protection
   (WREP), Hong Kong, PEOPLES R CHINA, JUN 07-08, 2014},
Abstract = {Take the example of Beijing, Tianjin and Shanghai and use the extended
   linear expenditure system model to analyze the residents' affordability
   for water price, the results show that the residents also have the
   capacity of the current water price and water price has space to rise.
   But for the low income groups its affordability reaches the limit, water
   price adjustments should consider the interests of this part.
   Implementation of water price ladder, not only it takes the water
   demands of social vulnerable groups into account, but also considers the
   market supply and demand. Charging high prices for high water
   consumption is in line with the principle of the more water, the more
   burdens. All that can promote water conservation and improve the
   utilization efficiency of water resources.},
