   Teknologi Bandung, Bandung, INDONESIA, APR 02-05, 2018},
Organization = {Inst Teknologi Bandung, Sch Architecture, Planning \& Policy Dev, Urban
   \& Reg Planning Study Program; Inst Teknologi Bandung, Res Ctr
   Infrastructure \& Reg Dev},
Abstract = {Access mode is an important factor in public transport systems. Most of
   the train users from Cicalengka to Padalarang via Bandung use
   paratransit as access mode. Access modes under this study are only
   paratransit and walking. This study aims to explore the relationship
   between access mode choice to the station and the perception about
   walking distance to station, perception about attributes of paratransit
   service quality which consist of accessibility, cheapness, comfortable,
   swiftness, safety, security and easiness. Of all the variables tested,
   walking distance to the station is the only variable relating to the
   mode access choice. So, a person will tend to use paratransit when
   his/her perception of walking distance to station is relatively far
   away. While perceptions about the quality of paratransit service can not
   determine whether a person will choose paratransit or not.},
