Note = {7th International Conference on Ecosystems and Sustainable Development,
   Chianciano Terme, ITALY, JUL 08-10, 2009},
Abstract = {Throughout the developed and the developing world, brownfield sites
   continue to be created, even while the inventory of these sites lag
   behind. In the city of Santa Cruz, Bolivia, abandoned brick factories
   have become illegal dumps that threaten human health, the environment,
   and ultimately the economic viability of the communities where they are
   located. This paper begins to examine the driving factors behind
   brownfields redevelopment in Bolivia. Perceived benefits of
   redevelopment projects are compared to gain a better understanding of
   the differences and similarities that may exist between developed and
   developing countries. A case study of a brownfield site in Santa Cruz is
   explored to highlight the connections between various types of risks and
   the desired social and economic values and ecological functions.},
