   Russian Acad Arts; Turkish Acad Sci; SGEM},
Abstract = {Several attempts seeking to explore national stereotypes have been made
   in the field of scientific research. Many of them dedicate themselves to
   a question of their relevance whether they are or are not true, or what
   is their truthfulness rate. National stereotypes are often perceived as
   simplified expression of existing ethnocentric and xenophobic
   prejudices; therefore they are being refused. Even though the national
   character stereotypes are somewhat distorted reality, a part of the true
   may be found in them, In shaping national, ethnic or other group myths,
   in particular two groups of auto-stereotype stereotypes (images and
   stereotypes about themselves) and hetero-stereotypes (pictures of the
   others, foreign) play an important role. This contribution aims to
   compare auto-stereotype notions of a typical member of the Slovak nation
   within the frame of selected research studies.},
