   MAR 26-30, 2006},
Organization = {Amer Chem Soc},
Abstract = {This study examined the possibility that variation in acceptability of
   sweeteners is due more to variation across individuals in sensitivity to
   non-sweet tastes rather than sensitivity to sweetness per se. Thirty
   individuals assessed 13 sweeteners, rating sweet, sour, salty, bitter
   and metallic intensities, as well as liking and acceptance. Results
   indicated that bitter intensity and sweetener type were the two largest
   factors contributing to liking and acceptance. Sensitivity to PROP did
   not contribute significantly to liking or acceptance.},
