   sociodemographic (age, sex) and medical characteristics (indication for
   surgery:  Chronic pancreatitis vs. pancreatic carcinoma; outcome after
   surgery:  diabetes, hypoglycemia, pain).  The relationships between ways
   of coping and several adaptation criteria were investigated.  The
   question is put up to discussion, if it is possible to clearly separate
   emotion as a way of coping and emotion as an outcome of coping.},
