   Int Commiss Ground Water; Int Assoc Hydrol Sci, Int Commiss Water Qual;
   Int Assoc Hydrol Sci, Int Commiss Continental Eros; Int Union Geodesy \&
   Geophys; Int Assoc Water Qual; Int Assoc Hydrgeol},
Abstract = {This paper presents a physically-based model (RISK-N) to simulate
   nitrogen cycling in soils, and nitrate transport and fate in soils and
   groundwater. The soil is separated into upper-root, lower-root,
   sub-drainfield, and intermediate vadose zones, each with uniform
   properties. Transport in each soil zone is modelled on the basis of
   complete mixing, by spatially averaging the related partial differential
   equation. Transport in the aquifer, however, is modelled using a
   two-dimensional advection-dispersion equation.},
