   Urban Hort; Univ Catania, Dept Agr, Food \& Environm; Natl Res Council,
   Res Inst Terrestrial Ecosystems; Int Soc Hort Sci, Working Grp Landscape
   Hort},
Abstract = {Nitrogen (N) is an essential nutrient for plants, and its application to
   crops in urban and rural areas may have a large impact on tree growth
   and yield, as well as on the environment. An experiment was performed in
   a peri-urban location in southwestern Puerto Rico to determine the
   effects rates and distribution of N fertilizer during the production
   cycle. `Butler' avocado trees growing in an open field were fertilized
   with different N regimens varying in the amount and time of N
   application. Trees fertilized with lower rates of N and/or with less
   frequent applications tended to be smaller and to have lower fruit
   yields. In comparison, fruit yield was greater when N applications were
   more frequent. Fruit yield depended on fruit number.},
