Note = {International Conference on Social Sciences and Education (ICSSE),
   Bandung, INDONESIA, NOV 21-23, 2017},
Abstract = {This study aimed to analyze the implementation of Shariah Accounting
   Standard, Reviewed from the Perception of The Accountants Candidate in
   Purwokerto. This study use a survey method with distributing the
   questionnaires to the respondent related implementation of Shariah
   Accounting Standard. Respondents are 83 students in Accounting Study
   Program in Faculty of Economic and Business University of Muhammadiyah
   Purwokerto. The data obtained was processed using descriptive ttatistic
   analysis. The Result showed that on average, 63\% respondents are very
   concern in Shariah Accounting Information. They say that the information
   content of financial statements in shariah accounting are more blessing,
   more shari, more fair, uphold the value of truth, nothing aberration,
   teaches simplicity and using Arabic terms. Information content of
   financial statements in shariah accounting can improve the quality of
   information for financial statement users. The results of research about
   the orientation of presentation of shariah accounting information is
   known that on average, almost 80\% of respondents have the orientation
   of presentation of shariah accounting information at shariah accounting
   is different when compared with conventional accounting. The other than,
   Shariah accounting are emphasizing religion, focus on maslahah, can be
   used by the society of non Muslim and can form the character of good
   governance. On average, there are more than 80\% of respondents perceive
   that shariah accounting is able to separate between halal and haram
   activities. Shariah accounting is considered to be able to avoid
   entities from uncertain and unclear transactions, eliminating riba,
   reducing unlawful and unfair economic practices. Islamic accounting can
   also able to give consideration to the guidance of Islam and welfare.},
