Note = {14th International Conference on Brain Informatics (BI), ELECTR NETWORK,
   SEP 17-19, 2021},
Abstract = {Over the past year, distance learning has become an integral part of our
   lives and a rapidly developing field. Compared to traditional classroom
   learning, online learning has advantages such as no place restrictions
   and a wide range of interactions. At the same time, distance learning
   lacks interaction between teachers and learners, and teachers cannot
   observe learners face to face. Identifying students' emotions during
   distance learning can have a positive impact on learning, improve
   learning outcomes and improve the effectiveness, quality of learning.
   This paper describes a theoretical model for determining
   sentiment/emotion from audio data based on speech recognition. The
   recognition model based on generalized transcription was proposed. This
   method can be used to determine the student's emotions during the
   distance learning and online exam.},
