Organization = {Inner Mongolia Univ},
Abstract = {In order to the search for more effective noise control measures and a
   more rational urban planning from the angle of economy, environment, so
   that we can create a healthier living environment, this paper does some
   preliminary investigation in the aspect of soundscape. This paper
   introduces soundscape science research status and research results
   domesticity and abroad, and on this basis, makes a subjective evaluation
   of voice of the landscape in Jiangxi Normal University, by combinating
   Psychoacoustic Evaluation Method. This paper record various of sounds
   existing in the campus, analyses properties of each sound, and does a
   large-scale survey about the popularity of these sounds. The paper
   chooses ten most popular voices using mark-giving method, and analyses
   the ten 10 kinds of sound by SD methods. The following are the results:
   (1) the ten most popular voices in the campus: voice of birds, sounds of
   musical instruments, voice of singing, reading, and teachers' lectures,
   and the sound of radio(music), broadcasting (in English and other
   programs), computer sound (music, film sound) and wind, 50\% of which
   are natural sounds, 30\% human voice, and 20\% noise of machines. From
   above, we can see that the sounds from nature are more acceptable. (2)
   By using semantic differential method (SD Act), the paper does a
   subjective evaluation on the ten popular kinds of voices. Marks are
   different form different analysing angle, that is, different people like
   different voices on different degrees. (3) When people work and learn,
   it is good to create some comfortable sounds in the surroundings and
   control or eliminate noisy sounds. Creating a comfortable sound
   surrounding environment is a good way to improve people' s working and
   learning efficiency. Sound landscape by sound (sound) and scape (King)
   is the auditory component of the Soundscape landscape, the landscape is
   sound, with a rich social and cultural connotations. It includes not
   only the sound pressure level, spectral analysis, reverberation time and
   other physical properties, but also with social, historical and
   environmental significance, etc., and based on the individual
   differences, value added and cultures have different meanings. Methods
   of landscape evaluation can be divided into: a detailed description
   method, the public preferred method (the first two non-quantitative
   methods, quantitative methods for the latter). Among them, the detailed
   description of model and ecological model, the public preference methods
   can be divided into mental models, cognitive models and comprehensive
   laws include psychophysical model. Acoustics is the scope of
   psychological discussion between the situation between subjective and
   objective, this evaluation is to consider the nature of the listener's
   subjective experience, whether that is the sound the listener's needs.
   Evaluation method according to the evaluation of the different tasks and
   requirements to determine, for the evaluation of tests using different
   corresponding methods of evaluation allows the theme of evaluation
   results more accurate and reliable. Psychoacoustic evaluation methods
   can be divided into: sorting method, paired comparison, score and
   semantic differential method. Campus landscape evaluation method for the
   evaluation of landscape visual quality approach to the visual guidance
   of factors, focusing on the landscape and view. The sound of this
   research is the landscape, the above method can be transplanted to the
   visual evaluation of the evaluations of hearing.
   Drawing on the visual landscape evaluation method for evaluation of
   hearing the sound landscape. The psycho-acoustic evaluation method takes
   into account the listener's subjective experience, that is, whether the
   sound needs of the listener. The evaluation focused on the acoustic
   sound of the landscape elements to evaluate the scene, so
   psycho-acoustic evaluation methods can be used for me. Campus scene
   elements in the sound itself has a rich variety of roles and different
   emotions, even if with one voice, in different scenes and people will
   feel different circumstances gives rise to different feelings. In this
   paper, Normal Yao Lake campus visit to discover the status of the
   investigation, the voice of campus composition is generally divided into
   natural sound, man-made sound, machine noise categories. Research
   literature to be taken, network data collection, surveys and other
   methods to understand the landscape of domestic and foreign sound
   research results, based on region-specific investigation, selection,
   evaluation methods to determine the sound landscape, and to propose the
   establishment of a good sound landscape of the campus recommendations.
   {[}GRAPHICS]
   The form of a questionnaire survey, questionnaire data using the score
   statistics major, that according to preference and annoyance, the sound
   of the five levels of each were used to form the corresponding points,
   like the count of 5, count is more like four, it does not matter counts
   as 3 points, several of the more annoying sense of 2 points, it is
   offensive counted as 1 point, and finally calculate the total score for
   each sound. Survey is Normal Yao Lake campus life of students, for no
   experience, no training of the respondents. The use of semantic
   differential method (SD method) is to allow the listener to use some of
   the pairs of polar adjectives (adjective of opposite meaning) to the
   subjective evaluation of sound samples.},
