   Virginia Beach, VA, OCT 18-20, 2012},
Organization = {Soc Christian Psychol},
Abstract = {This paper describes a basic psychological mechanism by which beliefs
   about God affect the structure of virtues in human beings. Iris Murdoch
   calls it the siege of the individual by concepts'. A premise is that
   appetites, desires, emotions, pleasures and pains have a conceptual
   dimension that can be trained by regular exposure to relevant concepts.
   Theological concepts are among the relevant ones. Another premise is
   that our virtues and vices are largely dispositions to appetites,
   desires, emotions, pleasures and pains. The argument is made by way of
   discussing two virtues, temperance and compassion.},
